    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1036">

                <pb facs="0778" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 125.8273/38c.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul General Hanna.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 4. Department is to-day sending appropriate telegraphic instructions to
                    Brazilian Minister at Mexico City. Telegraph all available information regarding
                    imprisonment of Silliman. Bonney and wife reported to-day safe in Mexico
                    City.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
